## Why This Is Asked
Tests for streaming pipelines are critical at scale; this angle emphasizes end-to-end guarantees, replay safety, and schema evolution beyond static REST tests.

## Key Concepts
- Streaming end-to-end testing with Kafka
- Exactly-once vs at-least-once semantics
- Windowed aggregations correctness
- Schema evolution and compatibility
- Backpressure and fault injection
- Canary deployments and CI validation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo test: idempotent ingestion with duplicate events
function testIdempotentIngestion() {
  const events = generateEvents({n: 1000, duplicates: true});
  ingest(events);
  ingest(events);
  const result = readWindowedAggStore();
  assert(result.latestWindowSum === expectedSum);
}
```

